{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Hecke.HeckeStaircase","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Hecke.HeckeStaircase","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Hecke.HeckeTower"],"declarations":13,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_mem_inclRange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_mem_inclRange","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L149-L157","doc":"**The generators below the top one lie in the tower subalgebra.**  `gen m`\nfor `m < n` is `incl (σ_m)`, so the whole closure argument's \"commute past\nand absorb\" cases land back in `(incl K q n).range`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_push_full","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_push_full","kind":"theorem","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L140-L147","doc":"**The full run, which is the case the old hypothesis missed.**  For\n`c_{n+1} = σ_n ⋯ σ_0` every generator except `σ_0` itself passes through.\nStated separately because it is the instance the closure argument's last\ncase needs, and the instance `n - k + 1 < i` would have excluded. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_push","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_push","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L97-L138","doc":"**A generator above the run's foot passes through with its index dropped.**\nThe Hecke analogue of `SymmetricCoxeter.t_push`.\n\nThe foot of `c_k = σ_n ⋯ σ_{n-k+1}` is `σ_{n+1-k}`, and `n + 1 - k` is the\nright way to write it: `n - k + 1` agrees for `k ≤ n` but is **off by one at\nthe full run** `k = n+1`, where truncated subtraction turns `n - (n+1) + 1`\ninto `1` while the actual foot is `σ_0`.  That would silently exclude\n`i = 1` from the last case of the closure argument, where it is needed and\nwhere it is true — at `n = 1`, `c₂ σ₁ = σ₁σ₀σ₁ = σ₀σ₁σ₀ = σ₀ c₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_fold","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_fold","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L89-L95","doc":"**Re-applying the run's last letter folds back**, at the cost of the only\ncoefficient in the whole argument. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_comm","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L79-L87","doc":"**A generator strictly below the run commutes past it.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_succ","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L76-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair_zero","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L74-L74","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.stair","kind":"def","line":69,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L69-L72","doc":"The descending run `c_k = σ_n σ_{n-1} ⋯ σ_{n-k+1}`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_comm","kind":"theorem","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L62-L67","doc":"The commutation relation, ℕ-indexed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_braid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_braid","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L53-L60","doc":"The braid relation, ℕ-indexed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_sq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_sq","kind":"theorem","line":47,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L47-L51","doc":"The quadratic relation, ℕ-indexed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_eq_σ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen_eq_σ","kind":"theorem","line":44,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L44-L45","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Hecke.IwahoriHecke.gen","kind":"def","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Hecke/HeckeStaircase.lean#L39-L42","doc":"`σ_m` for `m ≤ n`, and `1` above — an ℕ-indexed generator layer, so every\nside condition below is `omega`-shaped rather than `Fin`-shaped. ","signatureChunk":0}]}